  "description": "The East Coastway route opened in stages, starting as early as 1846, as part of the growing network sprouting out of Brighton - Britain’s first rail-served seaside town. Reaching Eastbourne 3 years later, followed by the Seaford branch in 1864, the line’s purpose has been simple and consistent for over 160 years - the mass movement of people (and goods) to and from key coastal locations."
